      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Los chacales escarbaban alrededor de las tumbas buscando comida. La gente les tenía miedo.",
          "en": "Jackals dug around the graves, looking for food. People were afraid of them."
        },
        {
          "es": "Muchos expertos creen que así empezó todo. Un dios chacal cuidaría las tumbas, en vez de escarbarlas.",
          "en": "Many experts think that is how it began. A jackal god would guard the graves, instead of digging them up."
        },
        {
          "es": "A Anubis lo pintaban de negro. Pero para los egipcios, el negro no era el color del mal.",
          "en": "Anubis was painted black. But for the Egyptians, black was not the color of evil."
        },
        {
          "es": "El negro era el color del barro fértil del Nilo, donde nace la vida nueva. Significaba renacer.",
          "en": "Black was the color of the rich mud of the Nile, where new life grows. It meant rebirth."
        }
      ],
